  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint : \r\n$\\mathrm{f}\\left[\\left(\\begin{array}{ll}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right)\\right]=4=\\mathrm{f}\\left[\\left(\\begin{array}{ll}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right)\\right]$\r\n$\\Rightarrow$ not one-one\r\nAs $0 \\in \\mathbb{R}$ but S does not contain any singular matrix so, $f$ is not onto",
